                "reply_count": 0,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Healthcare patients should not have to decide between delaying or prolonging treatment because of high costs. By cosponsoring the following three bipartisan bills, we are working to improve availability and access to healthcare services for those who need it most:\n\n\u25aa\ufe0fH.R. 2048, the Metastatic Breast Cancer Access to Care Act, a bill to waive arbitrary Social Security and Medicare waiting periods for eligible individuals with metastatic breast cancer because far too many individuals with this disease die waiting for their benefits.\n\n\u25aa\ufe0fThe Physician-Led and Rural Access to Quality Care Act is legislation to create a narrow exemption for physician-owned hospitals and increase access to care in rural areas where there is none.\n\nThe Prescription Information Modernization Act of 2025, legislation to allow for digital eLabeling, rather than paper, to become the standard for prescription drugs, allowing for smaller shipping packages and reduced waste.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1743450063,
                "view_count": 252
