                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 0,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "As Americans anxiously await seeing whether Congress will address health coverage, we are backing two bipartisan proposals that will implement reforms and keep costs down for many eastern North Carolina families.\n\n\u25aa\ufe0fH.R. 6501 Bipartisan Health Insurance Affordability Act, legislation to extend enhanced premium tax credits through 2027 to guard families against sudden increases in monthly premiums.\n\n\u25aa\ufe0fH.R. 6575 CommonGround for Affordable Health Care Act, a bill to include a two-year extension of health insurance premium savings for American families\u2014including a year of the enhanced Premium Tax Credits (ePTCs), with targeted modifications, new guardrails to prevent \u201cghost beneficiaries\u201d and crack down on fraud, an extension of open enrollment, and PBM reform.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1765830319,
                "view_count": 230
